nodecode-athletedata is a rewrite of athletedata-health's athletedata-health/mcp:

  https://github.com/athletedata-health/mcp
  commit 1ca2fa8d129c6b7c80a8af516a6653b7aa250679
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 HealthspanOS AG (LICENSE)

Rewritten: what the package is -- a front end to one hosted MCP server at
https://mcp.athletedata.health/mcp, reached with an API key, holding one
athlete's own training and health data from the apps they connected. The
manifest's facts became the cell's section (the endpoint, the key's
environment variable, the timeout) and the two verbs the server's own tool
set needs: one that lists it and one that calls into it, both speaking the
server's protocol (MCP over Streamable HTTP) with the core's own HTTP seam.
The skill's guidance -- start broad, drill into one provider, quote the
numbers, writes change the athlete's own accounts -- is the manual topic and
the tool descriptions, and the server's "untrusted, ask before a write"
posture became the confirm member: a tool the server does not mark read-only
refuses to run without it.

Left out, and why: the other manifests (server.json, gemini-extension.json,
.cursor-plugin/plugin.json, glama.json, clawhub/) name the same one endpoint
for other clients, and a cell needs one; build/build.mjs regenerates those
files from constants, which is the repository's own housekeeping and runs
nothing here. The skill is prose guidance in the manual rather than a
define-skill, so nothing is written into the operator's layer; and the
server's ~100 tool descriptions are not copied here, since the server serves
them at run time and a copy would go stale.
